#. §0: $m$
#: Game
msgid "# Welcome to the Number Theory Game\n"
"#### An introduction to integer arithmetic and formal proofs.\n"
"\n"
"In this game, we will explore the fascinating world of Number Theory.\n"
"We will start from the basic definition of divisibility and build our way up\n"
"to modular arithmetic and congruences.\n"
"\n"
"Our ultimate goal is to understand how remainders work, how to safely manipulate\n"
"equations modulo §0, and eventually reach powerful results like the\n"
"Chinese Remainder Theorem. We will do this by solving levels in a computer\n"
"puzzle game called Lean.\n"
"\n"
"# Read this.\n"
"\n"
"Learning how to use an interactive theorem prover takes time.\n"
"Tests show that the people who get the most out of this game are\n"
"those who read the help texts on the left side of the screen.\n"
"\n"
"To start, click on the **Divisibility Club**."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Problems.L01_large_powers
msgid "Huge Powers"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DivRules.L05_div9
msgid "Beautiful! Two lines of code prove a rule that feels like magic in middle school. Because polynomials preserve congruences, substituting 10 for 1 works perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DivRules.L07_div11
msgid "🎉 AMAZING! 🎉\n"
"\n"
"You have proven every major divisibility rule. What seemed like a list of random tricks in school is actually a beautiful, unified theory based on modular arithmetic and polynomials.\n"
"\n"
"You are now fully prepared. Take a deep breath — it is time to enter the final world, \"Problems\", where you will apply everything you've learned to crack actual numerical challenges!"
msgstr ""

