#. §14: $4$
#. §15: $12$
#. §16: $3 \\cdot 4 = 12$
#: Game.Doc.Theorems.LinCong
msgid "**Glued Modulus**\n"
"\n"
"If §0 and §1 with coprime moduli, then §2.\n"
"\n"
"**Intuition:**\n"
"§3 is a multiple of both §4 and §5 separately. If §6 and §7 share no common factor, the only way a number can be built from both is by being a multiple of their product §8 — nothing is double-counted. This is exactly why coprimality matters: if §9, a number could be a multiple of both without being a multiple of §10 (e.g. §11).\n"
"\n"
"**Example:** §12 is a multiple of both §13 and §14 (coprime!), and indeed §15 is a multiple of §16."
msgstr ""

