msgid "Let's start with the easiest rule: a number is divisible by 10 if and only if its last digit is 0.\n"
"\n"
"How do we write \"the last digit\" in math? Think about how numbers are built. You can split any number into its last digit and \"everything else\" multiplied by 10. For example, **347 = 34 * 10 + 7**.\n"
"So, any integer can mathematically be written as §0, where §1 is the last digit and §2 is the rest of the number.\n"
"\n"
"We want to prove that §3.\n"
"This is a direct consequence of §4 from World 2! You just need to massage the equation slightly."
msgstr ""

