#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "**Divisibility (§0)**\n"
"\n"
"We say that an integer §1 **divides** an integer §2 (written as §3) if §4 is a multiple of §5.\n"
"Formally, this means there exists some integer §6 such that:\n"
"§7\n"
"\n"
"**Intuition:**\n"
"Thinking of §8 as \"§9 can be built entirely out of copies of §10\" often makes it easier to reason about than the formal existential statement.\n"
"\n"
"**Examples:**\n"
"* §11 is true because §12 (here our witness is §13).\n"
"* §14 is true because §15 (here §16).\n"
"* §17 is true because §18 (here §19).\n"
"* §20 is **false**, because there is no integer §21 that makes §22.\n"
"\n"
"**How it works in Lean:**\n"
"When you see §23 in your goal, Lean translates this under the hood to an \\\\\"exists\\\\\" statement: §24.\n"
"To prove it, you must provide the exact value of §25 using the §26 tactic (for example, §27)."
