#: Game.Levels.LinCong.L10_crt_glue
msgid "Now prove that §0 divides §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Congruence.L06_mul
msgid "If two pairs of numbers are congruent, their products are congruent."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $0 \\le d_1$
#. §1: $0 \\le d_2$
#. §2: $d_1 \\mid d_2$
#. §3: $d_2 \\mid d_1$
#. §4: $d_1 = d_2$
#. §5: $\\mathbb{Z}$
#: Game.Doc.Theorems.GCD
msgid "**Antisymmetry of Divisibility (for non-negative integers)**\n"
"\n"
"If §0, §1, §2, and §3, then §4.\n"
"\n"
"**Why we need it:**\n"
"Divisibility on all of §5 only forms a *pre-order*: two different numbers can divide each other, as long as one is the negative of the other. Restricted to non-negative integers, though, divisibility becomes a genuine **partial order**: \"mutual divisibility\" really does collapse to equality.\n"
"\n"
"In this boss level, we will show two gcd-witnesses divide each other, and use exactly this theorem to conclude they must be the *same* number."
msgstr ""
